  "narrative": "All twelve delivered conditional main-effect results support their registered directions and clear the 0.15-unit scientific threshold with 95% Welch intervals entirely above the threshold. The signed estimates must be interpreted exactly as returned: for feature_037 claims (H44, H45, H56, H57), the positive signed values correspond to a raw negative feature_037-positive versus feature_037-negative contrast, i.e. stronger dependency; for feature_002 and feature_010 claims (H48-H51, H58-H61), the positive signed values correspond to raw positive contrasts, i.e. weaker dependency. The key finding is that none of the three strong marginal associations collapses when strata of another strong binary predictor are examined. Feature_037 remains associated with stronger dependency within both feature_002 strata and both feature_010 strata. Feature_002 remains associated with weaker dependency within both feature_037 strata and both feature_010 strata. Feature_010 remains associated with weaker dependency within both feature_037 strata and both feature_002 strata. Cell sizes are adequate for all Welch comparisons, with smallest exposed cells around 79-89. There is some apparent heterogeneity: feature_002 appears numerically larger in feature_010-positive strata (R29 estimate +0.990) than feature_010-negative strata (R30 +0.780), and feature_010 appears numerically larger in feature_002-positive strata (R31 +0.576) than feature_002-negative strata (R32 +0.367). However, these are overlapping stratum-specific contrasts, not formal interaction tests; confidence intervals overlap substantially, so I should not conclude amplification or masking yet. I therefore accept the conditional main-effect claims but close their direct investigations, while retaining formal interaction claims for follow-up. I request validation of H24 now because feature_002 is the strongest unvalidated accepted main association and validation would strengthen the basis for treating it as a robust dataset-specific effect. The next analytical priority should be the already registered pairwise interactions among feature_037, feature_002, and feature_010, especially the feature_002-by-feature_010 contrasts H54/H55, because the conditional estimates suggest possible effect modification that must be tested directly rather than inferred from overlapping subgroup effects.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted dataset claims: H19 feature_037 positive vs negative is accepted and validated (discovery signed +0.8325 CI +0.767/+0.898; validation +0.8166 CI +0.715/+0.918); H24 feature_002 positive vs negative accepted active and now requested for validation; H16 feature_010 positive vs negative accepted active, validation deferred. New accepted conditional claims, all closed as direct tests: feature_037 effect persists within feature_002 strata (H44 +0.809 CI +0.678/+0.940; H45 +0.832 CI +0.771/+0.893) and feature_010 strata (H56 +0.865 CI +0.644/+1.086; H57 +0.833 CI +0.779/+0.887); feature_002 effect persists within feature_037 strata (H48 +0.845 CI +0.714/+0.976; H49 +0.822 CI +0.761/+0.882) and feature_010 strata (H58 +0.990 CI +0.809/+1.171; H59 +0.780 CI +0.719/+0.841); feature_010 effect persists within feature_037 strata (H50 +0.412 CI +0.206/+0.618; H51 +0.444 CI +0.346/+0.542) and feature_002 strata (H60 +0.576 CI +0.414/+0.739; H61 +0.367 CI +0.265/+0.468). These are overlapping comparisons, not independent or multivariate estimates, but they argue against the simplest collapse of any one association into another predictor. Apparent heterogeneity is not formally established: H58 vs H59 and H60 vs H61 may suggest interaction, but intervals overlap. Next analyze batch should prioritize registered pairwise interactions: H46/H47 for feature_037 x feature_002, H52/H53 for feature_037 x feature_010, and especially H54/H55 for feature_002 x feature_010. Clinical feature_040 interactions H62-H67 remain deferred until top-predictor interaction evidence is clearer. Broad scan H25-H43 remains lower priority than resolving top-predictor dependence.",
