  "narrative": "The new validation resolves H24 decisively in the claimed direction. The returned validation estimate is already signed to H24, so R33 estimate +0.769 with high-confidence interval +0.676 to +0.862 means that, in the independent validation sample, feature_002=1 has a less negative composite dependency score than feature_002=0 by about 0.77 units, i.e. weaker dependency in this dataset. This is far above the 0.15-unit threshold and close to discovery R19 estimate +0.832, so I accept H24. I close H19 and H24 as direct main-effect investigations because their primary claims are supported; remaining uncertainty about mutual modification is handled by separate interaction claims. The H12 response deadline is also resolved against the claim: R13 is signed -0.052, opposite to the negative-direction hypothesis, with interval -0.150 to 0.046 crossing zero, while discovery R12 was only +0.107 with point estimate below threshold and upper bound barely above it. Together these refute a meaningful stronger-dependency association for feature_031 positive status, so H12 remains rejected and closed. Current best-supported main findings are feature_037 positivity with stronger dependency, validated for H19; feature_002 positivity with weaker dependency, validated for H24; and feature_010 positivity with weaker dependency, accepted for H16 but not yet independently validated. One-way conditional contrasts show persistence of each effect within strata of another top predictor, arguing against simple collapse into a single masking predictor, but they are overlapping unadjusted subgroup contrasts and do not establish independence, additive multivariable effects, mechanism, or generalizability. The apparent feature_002-feature_010 amplification requires formal interaction tests. The next analyses should prioritize the registered interaction claims H46/H47, H52/H53, and especially H54/H55. If meaningful positive interaction is found, interpret the main effects as dataset-specific joint/dependent associations; if interaction is not supported, treat them as separately associated but still noncausal predictors. After interaction testing, the most informative validation target is H16, followed by clinical log_pfs effect-modification tests and broader scans if capacity remains.",
  "research_notes": "Supported main findings after validation: H19 feature_037 positive vs negative associated with more negative composite dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency, accepted/validated and direct main investigation closed. H24 feature_002 positive vs negative associated with less negative score, i.e. weaker dependency, accepted/validated by R33 and direct main investigation closed. H16 feature_010 positive vs negative associated with weaker dependency remains accepted but active for possible validation. Refuted or null: H12 feature_031 negative-direction claim refuted by R13; feature_007/058/015, feature_041/048/023, and many other screened contrasts remain null or not scientifically meaningful. Conditional one-way persistence: feature_037 effects persist in feature_002 and feature_010 strata (H44/H45/H56/H57); feature_002 persists in feature_037 and feature_010 strata (H48/H49/H58/H59); feature_010 persists in feature_037 and feature_002 strata (H50/H51/H60/H61). These are not multivariable independence tests. Highest next priority: formal pairwise interactions, especially H54/H55 for feature_002 by feature_010 because R29/R30 and R31/R32 suggest apparent amplification; also H46/H47 and H52/H53 for feature_037 interactions. Then validate H16 if capacity permits. Clinical log_pfs feature_040 interactions H62-H67 remain deferred; broad H25-H43 are lower priority. All claims remain dataset-specific associations, not causal effects or generalizable biological claims."
